                "senses": [
                    {
                        "sense_id": "df58acce-8156-355a-8414-e551b17a3730",
                        "entry_id": "119a6be0-b4d6-3a88-90e4-abc88418c42d",
                        "glosses": [
                            "Misogynie racialisée envers les femmes noires."
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "66aae2c5-3f49-48df-9cb4-219de4247a37",
                                "sense_id": "df58acce-8156-355a-8414-e551b17a3730",
                                "text": "La misogynoir est le terme pour qualifier une misogynie spécifique visant les femmes noires, et produite par les hommes en général – indépendamment de leur couleur de peau, donc."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "25e4884b-b40a-4e13-b862-f19478f0cbfc",
                                "sense_id": "df58acce-8156-355a-8414-e551b17a3730",
                                "text": "Cette spécificité des oppressions sexistes-racistes-coloristes que vivent les femmes noires a un nom : la misogynoir théorisée par Moya Bailey, universitaire queer noire américaine."
                            }
                        ]
                    }
                ],
                "translations": [
                    {
                        "translation_id": "fe3e8228-3edf-4f72-84f4-437107446089",
                        "source_entry_id": "119a6be0-b4d6-3a88-90e4-abc88418c42d",
                        "source_sense_id": "df58acce-8156-355a-8414-e551b17a3730",
                        "target_lang_word": "misogynoir",
                        "target_lang_code": "en",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "misogynoir",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "c003caca-1944-3a3f-b3c0-efb4a01e77fc",
                                        "entry_id": "c91612e9-1777-38e0-81ad-316f62c07804",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Contempt for, hatred of, or prejudice against black women."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "neologism",
                                            "uncountable"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "73dd9745-2b86-465f-9c7f-61d1b2a242f5",
                                                "sense_id": "c003caca-1944-3a3f-b3c0-efb4a01e77fc",
                                                "text": "My reorientation to the misogynoir ruling the radio took place when I tried to make the argument that “All the Way Turnt Up” was a great song because it didn’t objectify women. This was something I could get behind; a song simply extolling the youthful value of keeping the bass bumping in your vehicle. That was until I read the lyrics and found the choice lyric “three dike bitches, and they all wanna swallow.”"
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "ad92d051-3232-4ba3-9328-1d021f3f7388",
                                                "sense_id": "c003caca-1944-3a3f-b3c0-efb4a01e77fc",
                                                "text": "Hip-hop feminist studies continues to tackle black sexual politics by discussing and challenging the persistence and prevalence of hip-hop \"misogynoir\" (the hatred of black women and girls), respectability politics, and compulsory heterosexuality within the music and the culture at large."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "d50611b6-d4c3-4836-97a0-b8ba8c85ace7",
                                                "sense_id": "c003caca-1944-3a3f-b3c0-efb4a01e77fc",
                                                "text": "Unfortunately, the idealization of white women is most often paired with the condemnation of black women, creating the intersectional problem of misogynoir: the combined racism and sexism black women face."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "142483c0-b0bc-409c-b9a3-f33ca20355df",
                                                "sense_id": "c003caca-1944-3a3f-b3c0-efb4a01e77fc",
                                                "text": "Drawing upon a history in which racism, heteropatriarchy, and inter-racial gender ideology rendered Black women invisible and marginalized, Pough compels Black feminists attempting to reject hip-hop feminism to revisit the historical record of Black women pushing back against Black male sexism and misogynoir in Black political, cultural, and social spaces."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "03653e45-4afa-42ee-978a-0afaed5076c3",
                                                "sense_id": "c003caca-1944-3a3f-b3c0-efb4a01e77fc",
                                                "text": "[A] Black woman as the arbiter of racialized sexism against a young Black girl is an example of misogynoir."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "8efa6c77-2220-4aa5-9b41-727b62c8629a",
                                                "sense_id": "c003caca-1944-3a3f-b3c0-efb4a01e77fc",
                                                "text": "To me, his words seemed a form of “misogynoir” – discrimination prejudice, and violence aimed specifically at women of colour."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
                    }
                ],
